# One document, two formats

```sh
./book/build.sh
```

→ `book/out/heat-and-hot-water.html` **and** `book/out/heat-and-hot-water.pdf`

That is the only report. Both formats are intentional. Do not create parallel guides or alternate output names.

**Part one** (Tyrah): `book/00`–`05` + `book/install-in-this-order.md` — plain English, install path, living with it.

**Part two** (appendix): `book/front-matter.md`, `book/appendix/*`, `book/research/*` — numbers, sources, open items.

# Breadth then depth

## Phase A — Breadth

1. Walk part one end-to-end.
2. Official names everywhere (Hydronic D5S diesel heater, Sure Marine cabin heater, Duda B3-12DW-20 plate heat exchanger, Isotemp Slim Square 4.2 gal heat battery, WFT 5 L expansion/header tank, EasyStart Timer, AM100-1LF thermostatic mixing valve, Altitude kit 22 1000 33 22 00).
3. One loop story: diesel heater → cabin heater → plate → heat-battery coil → back. No engine connection. Heat-battery chamber is static glycol; factory mixer unused.
4. Rebuild; skim HTML and PDF. Fix contradictions before deepening.

## Phase B — Depth

1. Deepen one section at a time.
2. Keep install serial — no mid-step design essays.
3. Put verified facts in plain language in part one; cite SRC/DEC in part two.
4. Rebuild both formats after each pass.

# Voice (part one)

Conversational, calm, precise. Stop rules when harm is real. No open-question tables or leftover heater-family comparisons in part one.

# Context cost

Default work is under `book/**/*.md` and `book/diagrams/*`. Do not open `photos/`, manufacturer PDFs, `book/out/`, or `book/vendor/` unless the user asks for a specific file. Cite paths instead of pasting binaries.
